 "notices": [
  {
   "id": "USN-9183-1",
   "title": "Linux kernel (FIPS) vulnerabilities",
   "summary": "Several security issues were fixed in the Linux kernel.\n",
   "instructions": "After a standard system update you need to reboot your computer to make\nall the necessary changes.\n\nATTENTION: Due to an unavoidable ABI change the kernel updates have\nbeen given a new version number, which requires you to recompile and\nreinstall all third party kernel modules you might have install",
   "references": [],
   "published": "2026-11-20T15:34:40.507881",
   "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - USB Gadget drivers;\n  - Memory management;\n  - Multiple devices driver;\n  - Network file systems library;\n  - Networking core;\n  - eXpress Data Path;\n  - Stream parser;\n  - Kernel build system;\n  - ARM32 architecture;\n  - ARM64 architecture;\n  - M68K architecture;\n  - MIPS architecture;\n  - OpenRISC architecture;\n  - PowerPC architecture;\n  - RISC-V architecture;\n  - S390 architecture;\n  - User-Mode Linux (UML);\n  - x86 architecture;\n  - Block layer subsystem;\n  - Intel NPU Driver;\n  - Compute Acceleration Framework;\n  - Speakup Console Speech Driver;\n  - ACPI drivers;\n  - Android drivers;\n  - Serial ATA and Parallel ATA drivers;\n  - Auxiliary display drivers;\n  - Drivers core;\n  - Micron PCIe SSD driver;\n  - Null block device driver;\n  - Ublk userspace block driver;\n  - Compressed RAM block device driver;\n  - Bluetooth drivers;\n  - Bus devices;\n  - AMD CDX bus driver;\n  - Hardware random number generator core;\n  - Character device driver;\n  - TPM device driver;\n  - Clock framework and drivers;\n  - Clocksource drivers;\n  - CPU frequency scaling framework;\n  - CPU idle management framework;\n  - Hardware crypto device drivers;\n  - CXL (Compute Express Link) drivers;\n  - DAX dirext access to differentiated memory framework;\n  - Buffer Sharing and Synchronization framework;\n  - DMA engine subsystem;",
   "is_hidden": false,
   "release_packages": {
